Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_wait_returns_at_the_first_reading_past_its_deadline`.

The defect: a wait gives up only when the clock lands exactly on its deadline, so a clock that
steps past it (any real clock read at an arbitrary moment) never ends the wait, and a dead
controller hangs the driver.

Expected to fail: `the driver read the clock again after its deadline had passed`, in the
adversarial clock.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
@@ -331,7 +331,7 @@
             if done(&mut self.registers) {
                 return true;
             }
-            if self.registers.now_microseconds().wrapping_sub(start) > deadline_microseconds {
+            if self.registers.now_microseconds().wrapping_sub(start) == deadline_microseconds {
                 return done(&mut self.registers);
             }
         }
